<title>USA: IDB okays $1.5 mln environmental grant to Guyana.</title>
<headline>IDB okays $1.5 mln environmental grant to Guyana.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Inter-American Development Ban (IDB) announced on Thursday that it had approved a $1.5 million grant to Guyana to bolster its new Environmental Protection Agency.</p>
<p>The funds, which will also be used by the Guyana Forestry Commission and the Geology and Mines Commission, are intended to help the government develop laws and regulations to protect and manage natural resources.</p>
<p>The bank also approved a $990,000 grant to pay for legal and technical advisory services to help the government move ahead with privatizing the state power company, Guyana Electricity Corp.</p>
</text>
